From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 17:38:20 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] initcpio: Add apple_nvmem_spmi module

The SPMI nvmem support was merged upstream as apple_nvmem_spmi in v6.16,
replacing the downstream simple-mfd-spmi + nvmem_spmi_mfd pair. The
dracut module picked up the new name in 8215ce8 ("dracut: Add
apple_spmi_nvmem module"), but the mkinitcpio hook still lists only the
old pair, so on a kernel that builds NVMEM_APPLE_SPMI as a module the
provider of the PMIC rtc_offset cell never reaches the initramfs.
rtc-macsmc then defers until the root filesystem's udev loads the
provider, and the initramfs runs without a valid wall clock.

Add apple_nvmem_spmi next to rtc-macsmc and spmi-apple-controller, and
keep the old modules for older kernels, as the dracut module does.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 initcpio/install/asahi | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/initcpio/install/asahi b/initcpio/install/asahi
index 304b91f..31730ac 100644
--- a/initcpio/install/asahi
+++ b/initcpio/install/asahi
@@ -24,8 +24,9 @@ build() {
     map add_module spi-apple? spi-hid-apple? spi-hid-apple-of?
 
     # For RTC
-    map add_module rtc-macsmc? simple-mfd-spmi? spmi-apple-controller? \
-        nvmem_spmi_mfd?
+    map add_module rtc-macsmc? spmi-apple-controller? apple_nvmem_spmi?
+    # pre upstream spmi nvmem, delete with 6.16 + 1 release
+    map add_module simple-mfd-spmi? nvmem_spmi_mfd?
 
     # For MTP HID
     map add_module apple-dockchannel? dockchannel-hid? apple-rtkit-helper?
-- 
2.56.0

